n using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn6le05ob04re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Consonant Blends St Sound"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Consonant clusters like st can occur at the beginning of a word in English."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Practice blending the sound from one consonant sound into the next without adding a vowel sound in between.<br><br>Read the following words aloud.<br><br>Example:<br>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"storm\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"stage\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"stun\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"stump\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"story\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"stove\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"student\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"stub\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Stressing New Information"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Sentence stress gives English its <span class=\"strong\">rhythm</span> or \"beat\". "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Word stress is emphasis on <span class=\"strong\">one syllable</span> within a <span class=\"strong\">word</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Sentence stress is emphasis on <span class=\"strong\">certain words</span> within a <span class=\"strong\">sentence</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Most sentences have two basic types of words:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Content Words</span> <br><ul><li>Content words are the important or key words in a sentence. They provide the meaning of the sentence</li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Structure Words</span> <br><ul><li>Structure words are not important words. They are small words that you use to make the sentence correct. </li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:<span class=\"italic\"> <span class=\"strong\">I</span> do <span class=\"strong\">not want</span> to <span class=\"strong\">stay</span>.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "The content words are in bold."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Stressing New Information</span><br>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You pronounce information that is new with stress, since it is more important to the listener. <br/>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example: <br/><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Sara</span>: Where do you come from? <br/><span class=\"strong\">Sonya</span>: I'm from <span class=\"strong\">London</span>.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "The fact that Sonya is from London is new to Sara, thus it is stressed."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "energy"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "ability to be active "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Your child has a lot of energy."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le05ob04aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you hear in a conversation at a restaurant."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to stomp "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to step on very forcefully "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: That child just stomped on my foot.